==== Serial ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

The VR900v 1.0 has at least 3 different serial interfaces, all of which seem to use the same voltage, pinout.

All interfaces can be populated by soldering in standard 2.54mm pin headers, although at least on my board, the GND pin on all 3 interfaces would //not// accept any solder. You may want to carefully sand or brass-brush the GND pins before soldering to remove the (invisible/transparent) lacquer. Please note that this problem only affects the GND pins and **not** the TX/RX/VCC pins.

{{media:tplink:vr900v:vr900v-v1.0_pcb_serial.jpg?direct&200 |}}

^ Serial connection parameters for TP-Link Archer VR900v 1.0 ^^^^^
^ Serial port on PCB ^ Voltage ^ Pinout\\ (starting from the squared pin) ^ Connection parameters ^ Notes ^
^ J4  | 3.3V | TX, RX, GND, VCC | 115200, 8N1 | Normal Linux shell\\ default login data with stock firmware:\\ admin : 1234 |
^ J7 | 3.3V | TX?, RX?, GND, VCC | unknown, 8N1? | Function and baud rate unknown yet |
^ J8 | 3.3V | TX, RX, GND, VCC | 115200, 8N1 | Some strange debugging shell\\ default login data with stock firmware:\\ admin : //<empty password>// |
